@page "/video-face-review"
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>Video face review · Photo Identity</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Video library · experimental review</p>
        <h1>Video face review</h1>
        <p>Review private face candidates in the existing application. Confirm a known person from a single crop, classify unknown or false detections, or leave groups unreviewed.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/videos">Back to videos</a>
</section>

<section class="vfr-intro" aria-label="Private video review import">
    <h2>Load a private evidence package</h2>
    <p>Use the <code>presence-first-web-review.json</code> created by the explicit WI-0155 offline <code>-PresenceFirst</code> runner. This package contains personal face crops. Select it only in your trusted local Photo Identity browser; it is read in browser memory and is not sent to the server.</p>
    <label class="vfr-import">
        <span>Private review package (JSON)</span>
        <input id="vfr-bundle" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" />
    </label>
    <input id="vfr-csv" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv" hidden aria-label="Import saved review CSV" />
    <p id="vfr-load-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No private evidence loaded.</p>
    <p>Known-person suggestions are unverified leads. Confirm only with the same private people-alias map used by the offline experiment. Export a CSV before leaving: the application does not retain decisions, enrol video faces, contact inference services, or create production video/person assignments.</p>
</section>

<div id="vfr-root" class="vfr-root"></div>

@code {
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("photoIdentityVideoFaceReview.init");
    }
}
